// Short-Term Oscillator · Dan-style bands
// A market-timing gauge in the spirit of Dan Zanger's short-term oscillator:
// a centered momentum reading for the NASDAQ, judged against HIS bands —
// above +35 = overbought, below -40 = oversold (his numbers, from his material).
//
// Construction (standard, stated openly — this is NOT Dan's proprietary
// ChartPattern formula, which is not public):
//   oscillator = CCI(8) of the source index's daily typical price x 0.228,
//   clipped to +/-50.
//
// REFIT 2026-10-14, anchored on Dan's first stated print: his oscillator
// closed at -40 on 2026-10-14 ("oversold conditions begin at -40 and
// lower"). CCI(8) on QQQ printed -175.5 that day, so scale 0.228 solves
// the gauge to exactly -40 at that close. Why CCI: it self-normalizes by
// recent mean deviation, so it stays moderate through calm uptrends yet
// plunges on a sudden cascade — the behavior Dan's readings show. Fitted
// band behavior on QQQ daily history (Oct 2021 - Oct 2026, 1,254 bars):
// above +35 on ~5.5% of days, below -40 on ~2.5%, pinned at the clip on
// ~0.6%. Readings for the anchor week: Oct 7 +16, Oct 8 +1, Oct 9 +1,
// Oct 12 -15, Oct 13 -33, Oct 14 -40. Sanity check on SPY (not fitted):
// -32 on 2026-10-14 — less oversold than QQQ, matching SPY's milder drop.
// The previous construction (10-day ROC x 5) read only -7.3 on 2026-10-14
// and was retired: a 10-day window is still digesting the prior two weeks
// when a fast washout reaches the band. An earlier fit attempt across ROC,
// RSI-centered, deviation, net-up-days and z-score families confirmed the
// pattern: only the self-normalizing CCI family satisfies both band
// frequencies at the anchor-exact scale.
// HONEST LIMIT: this fit rests on ONE anchor print plus band-frequency
// behavior — a behavioral match, not Dan's formula. Further stated prints
// will validate it or force a revision; if his prints disagree
// systematically, adjust the Scale input — one number.
//
// The gauge reads the source symbol's DAILY series (default QQQ) on any
// chart and any timeframe — the CCI is computed inside the daily security
// request, so it shows the same number everywhere. On intraday charts the
// current day's reading is a live estimate until the close.

//@version=6
indicator("Short-Term Oscillator · Dan-Style Bands", shorttitle = "ST Osc", overlay = false, precision = 1)

srcSym   = input.symbol("NASDAQ:QQQ", "Source symbol", group = "Oscillator")
useChart = input.bool(false, "Use chart symbol instead of source", group = "Oscillator")
cciLen   = input.int(8, "CCI length (days)", minval = 2, group = "Oscillator")
scale    = input.float(0.228, "Scale", minval = 0.01, step = 0.001, group = "Oscillator")
obLevel  = input.float(35.0, "Overbought band", group = "Oscillator")
osLevel  = input.float(-40.0, "Oversold band", group = "Oscillator")

sym = useChart ? syminfo.tickerid : srcSym

f_osc() =>
    ta.cci(hlc3, cciLen) * scale

oscRaw = request.security(sym, "D", f_osc())
osc = math.max(-50.0, math.min(50.0, oscRaw))

oscColor = osc >= obLevel ? color.new(color.red, 0) : osc <= osLevel ? color.new(color.lime, 0) : color.new(color.gray, 0)
plot(osc, "Oscillator", color = oscColor, linewidth = 2)
hline(obLevel, "Overbought", color = color.new(color.red, 40), linestyle = hline.style_dashed)
hline(0, "Zero", color = color.new(color.gray, 60), linestyle = hline.style_dotted)
hline(osLevel, "Oversold", color = color.new(color.lime, 40), linestyle = hline.style_dashed)
bgcolor(osc >= obLevel ? color.new(color.red, 88) : osc <= osLevel ? color.new(color.lime, 88) : na, title = "Band zones")
